condition_name: Peptic Ulcer Disease (PUD)
condition_slug: peptic-ulcer-disease-pud
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: "Peptic ulcers (gastric, duodenal or lower oesophagus) are defects in the gastrointestinal mucosa that extend through the muscularis mucosa."
clinical_features[1]:
  - type: Clinical Features
    features[4]: Recurrent epigastric pain,Often radiating to the back,Worse at night,Improved by antacids
investigations[4]: Occult blood test. Stool microscopy,Endoscopy,Barium meal,Direct/indirect detection of H. pylori
treatment:
  goals[4]: Relieve pain,Promote healing of ulcers,Eradicate H. pylori,Prevent/reduce recurrence
  non_drug[0]:
  drug[6]: H. pylori eradication,"Triple therapy with: Clarithromycin 500 mg orally every 12 hours for 10 - 14 days","Plus: Amoxicillin 1g orally every 12 hours for 10-14 days","Plus: Omeprazole 20 mg orally every 12 hours for 10 - 14 days","Omeprazole could be substituted with other proton pump inhibitors (PPI) e.g. rabeprazole, rantoprazole or esomeprazole.","If no improvement with the above regimen, patient should be referred to a Gastroenterologist for further evaluation and therapy."
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[1]: "Gastric irritation, diarrhoea from triple therapy"
  supportive_measures[2]: Regular meals,"Avoidance of provocative factors (NSAIDs, alcohol, spicy foods etc.)"
differential_diagnoses[0]:
complications[4]: Upper gastrointestinal bleeding,Perforation,Penetration,Gastric outlet obstruction
prevention[0]:
other_investigations: null
definitive_treatment: null
prognosis: null